---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Gallery title="Offline & queued actions">
  <p class="demo-note">
    What this framework ships for flaky-network ERP reality — and, stated
    just as plainly, what it deliberately does not. The split is the same
    one every page here follows: <strong>the framework does visuals and
    contracts; the queue engine, storage and replay are your app's</strong>
    (the reference products sell session persistence as a <em>server</em>;
    a CSS framework pretending to ship it would be selling air).
    <strong>Not a promise of offline-first</strong> — if your deployment
    needs true offline capture, that is an application architecture
    (service worker, local store, idempotent replay) this page gives you
    the <em>visible half</em> of, nothing more.
  </p>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>The four states a user must be able to tell apart</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">Chip</th><th scope="col">Announced</th><th scope="col">Meaning for the user</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Online</td>
            <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--success"><span aria-hidden="true">●</span> Online</span></td>
            <td>"Connection: online"</td>
            <td>acting saves now</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Syncing</td>
            <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--accent"><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> Syncing</span></td>
            <td>"Connection: syncing changes"</td>
            <td>recent work is in flight; leaving now may lose the tail</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Queued</td>
            <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--warning"><span aria-hidden="true">⏸</span> 3 queued</span></td>
            <td>"Connection: offline, 3 actions queued"</td>
            <td>work is captured, not saved — the COUNT is the honesty: "offline" alone hides how much is at risk</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Error</td>
            <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--danger"><span aria-hidden="true">✕</span> Sync error</span></td>
            <td>"Connection: sync failed, retry needed"</td>
            <td>replay hit something a retry alone will not fix — this state must never decay back to a quiet glyph</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Every state is <strong>two-channel by
    shape</strong>: the glyph differs in FORM (● ↻ ⏸ ✕), never only in
    colour, and the text says the state in words. Changes are announced
    through one <code>aria-live="polite"</code> region beside the chip —
    polite, because a connection blip mid-sentence is context, not an
    emergency. Zero new CSS: this is
    <a href={base + '/components/badge'}>badge</a> composition, and the
    slot's fixed home is the
    <a href={base + '/patterns/app-frame'}>app frame's</a> top bar — a
    status that moves between screens is a status users stop finding.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>The contract your queue engine owes the chip</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Rule</th><th scope="col">Why</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Both channels move in one place, together</td><td>a chip that says Online while the live region still says queued is worse than either alone</td></tr>
          <tr><td>The queued state carries the count</td><td>"3 queued" is a fact the user can weigh before walking out of wifi range; "offline" is a mood</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Queued actions must be idempotent on replay</td><td>a reconnect that re-posts a claim or a scan twice turns signalling into data corruption; design the server so replay is safe (the same 409 discipline every pattern here documents)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Error is sticky until acted on</td><td>auto-clearing a failed sync teaches users the red state means nothing</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Screens stay honest about what is local</td><td>a row that exists only in the queue renders with a queued cue (a <a href={base + '/components/badge'}>badge</a>), not disguised as saved — the RF pages' session-lost rows follow the same rule</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Related links={[
    ["/patterns/app-frame", "App frame (the slot's fixed home)"],
    ["/patterns/goods-receipt", "Goods receipt (session-lost, honestly)"],
    ["/concepts/concurrency", "Concurrency & conflicts (the 409 discipline replay relies on)"],
    ["/components/badge", "Badge"],
  ]} />
</Gallery>
